のですが、どのようにこちらのチャットに指示を出せばできますか？\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Core Requests**:\n  1. **Period Sweep Execution**: For 2H-SiC $\\{10\\bar{1}0\\}$ natural cleavage slab models with vacuum layer $5.0\\text{ \\AA}$, calculate the missing period counts: **1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10 周期** (completing the full 1〜10 series alongside existing 2, 4, 6, 8 periods).\n  2. **Mandatory Bulk-First Protocol (AGENTS.md §1)**: For each period count $N$, conduct the true bulk 1-point SCF calculation ($36 \\times N$ atoms, $L_z = N \\times 2.6639\\text{ \\AA}$, 0 Å vacuum) **first** to determine $E_{\\text{bulk}}(N)$ and verify energy-per-atom consistency ($\\approx -443.5\\text{ eV/atom}$), write $E_{\\text{bulk}}(N)$ to metadata, and only then proceed to the slab structural relaxation.\n  3. **Analysis Conditions (Identical to Recent Runs)**:\n     - Quantum ESPRESSO 7.6: `ecutwfc = 40.0 Ry`, `ecutrho = 320.0 Ry`, `conv_thr = 1.0e-5 Ry`, $\\Gamma$-point, `mixing_beta = 0.3`.\n     - Optimization: `minimize 1.0e-6 1.0e-2 100 150` (AGENTS.md §9).\n     - Parallelism: 24 threads (`12 MPI × 2 OpenMP`) via `prterun`/`mpirun` on Intel Core Ultra 9 285K + RTX 5080.\n     - Element mapping: Type 1 = C (12.011), Type 2 = Si (28.085).\n  4. **Data Bundling & NAS Destination**:\n     - NAS Destination: `\\\\192.168.12.69\\Results\\yamazaki\\research\\{101_0}〇周期5Å` (where `〇` $\\in \\{1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10\\}$).\n     - **Requirement**: Each period's folder must include **both** the slab calculation data (`log.lammps`, `espresso.pwo`, `md_animation.xyz`, 3 progression graphs, `fracture_metadata.json`) **and** the bulk calculation data (`espresso_bulk_scf.pwi`, `espresso_bulk_scf.pwo`, `bulk_10-10_{natoms}atoms_true_bulk.*`).\n  5. **Automation Inquiry**: Explain to the user how to prompt the chat to automate this period-sweep calculation workflow (specifically via `/goal`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Previous Turns**:\n  1. **2-Period Vacuum Sweep (0.5 Å 〜 10.0 Å, 0.5 Å steps, 20 conditions)**: 100% completed, staged, and backed up to NAS `\\\\192.168.12.69\\Results\\yamazaki\\research\\{101_0}2周期〇Å` (37 files each).\n  2. **Small Vacuum Sweep (0.75 Å, 0.25 Å, 0.0 Å, 3 conditions)**: Completed via [`run_2periods_small_vacuum_sweep.py`](file:///home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/run_2periods_small_vacuum_sweep.py), staged, and synced to NAS:\n     - `{101_0}2周期0.75Å`: $E_{\\text{slab}} = -31,934.5092\\text{ eV}$, $\\Delta E = 0.8480\\text{ eV}$, $\\gamma = \\mathbf{0.0486\\text{ J/m}^2}$ (potential minimum, near-perfect bulk recombination).\n     - `{101_0}2周期0.25Å`: $E_{\\text{slab}} = -31,872.4811\\text{ eV}$, $\\Delta E = 62.8761\\text{ eV}$, $\\gamma = \\mathbf{3.6043\\text{ J/m}^2}$ (inter-slab compressive repulsion).\n     - `{101_0}2周期0Å`: $E_{\\text{slab}} = -31,796.2057\\text{ eV}$, $\\Delta E = 139.1515\\text{ eV}$, $\\gamma = \\mathbf{7.9766\\text{ J/m}^2}$ (extreme steric repulsion barrier).\n  3. **Master Summary & 4 Default Specification Graphs**:\n     - Generated with all 23 vacuum conditions (0.0 Å to 10.0 Å):\n       - `真空層の厚さと表面破壊エネルギーの関係_デフォルト仕様.*` ($0.0 \\sim 5.0\\text{ J/m}^2$, 5.6×4.4\", 300 dpi)\n       - `真空層の厚さと表面破壊エネルギーの関係_全域表示仕様.*` ($0.0 \\sim 9.0\\text{ J/m}^2$, full range including 0.0 Å)\n       - `真空層の厚さと表面破壊エネルギーの関係_Word最適化仕様.*` (8.0×6.2 cm, 600 dpi)\n       - `真空層の厚さと表面破壊エネルギーの関係_プラトー拡大仕様.*` ($2.2 \\sim 3.2\\text{ J/m}^2$, zoom on plateau)\n     - All 4 formats (PNG, PDF, SVG) and summary CSVs synced to NAS root via [`copy_summary_to_nas.py`](file:///home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/copy_summary_to_nas.py).\n  4. **Period Sweep Preparation**:\n     - Built master automation script [`run_periods_sweep_1_to_10.py`](file:///home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/run_periods_sweep_1_to_10.py).\n     - Verified ASE geometry for $N \\in \\{1, 2, \\dots, 10\\}$: unit cell generates $4N$ atoms ($36N$ atoms in $3\\times 3$), exactly $2N$ atomic layers, with dense pairs preserved at both ends and natural cleavage weak bonds ($dz \\approx 1.776\\text{ \\AA}$) externally. Bulk minimum distance across boundaries is confirmed to be $1.8845\\text{ \\AA}$ (exact tetrahedral Si-C bond length) for all $N$.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Physics of Small Vacuum Layers**:\n  - $0.75\\text{ \\AA}$ vacuum corresponds to inter-slab gap $2 \\times 0.75 = 1.50\\text{ \\AA}$, nearly equal to the bulk weak bond spacing of $1.776\\text{ \\AA}$, yielding $\\gamma = 0.0486\\text{ J/m}^2 \\approx 0$ (energy minimum).\n  - Vacuum $< 0.75\\text{ \\AA}$ enters the steep Pauli repulsion wall ($0.25\\text{ \\AA} \\implies 3.60\\text{ J/m}^2$, $0.0\\text{ \\AA} \\implies 7.98\\text{ J/m}^2$).\n- **Period Scaling & Compute Requirements**:\n  - $N=1$: 36 atoms (Bulk: ~15 s, Slab: ~2 min)\n  - $N=3$: 108 atoms (Bulk: ~40 s, Slab: ~8 min)\n  - $N=5$: 180 atoms (Bulk: ~2 min, Slab: ~20 min)\n  - $N=7$: 252 atoms (Bulk: ~4 min, Slab: ~40 min)\n  - $N=9$: 324 atoms (Bulk: ~8 min, Slab: ~65 min)\n  - $N=10$: 360 atoms (Bulk: ~12 min, Slab: ~85 min)\n  - Total sequential runtime for all 6 conditions is estimated at **3.5〜4.5 hours**.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **PowerShell Encoding & LiteralPath**:\n  - *Error*: Passing Japanese path literals directly on bash command line corrupted characters.\n  - *Fix*: Encode PowerShell scripts as Base64 UTF-16LE (`-EncodedCommand`) from Python scripts.\n- **PowerShell Output Encoding on Japanese Windows**:\n  - *Error*: `UnicodeDecodeError: 'utf-8' codec can't decode byte 0x90` in `copy_summary_to_nas.py` because PowerShell stdout is CP932 (Shift-JIS).\n  - *Fix*: Decode stdout with `.decode(\"cp932\", errors=\"replace\")`.\n- **OpenMPI Single-Copy IPC in Linux Sandbox**:\n  - *Error*: Direct invocation of `mpirun` without `OMPI_MCA_btl_vader_single_copy_mechanism=none` caused `pw.x` to hang at startup.\n  - *Fix*: Always export `OMPI_MCA_btl_vader_single_copy_mechanism=none`.\n- **Python Environment Path**:\n  - *Error*: Default system `python3` (Python 3.14) lacks packages (`matplotlib`, `ase`, `mdi`).\n  - *Fix*: Always invoke `/home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_env_rtx5080/bin/python3`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Prepared Master Script**: [`run_periods_sweep_1_to_10.py`](file:///home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/run_periods_sweep_1_to_10.py)\n  - Implements Phase 1 (True Bulk SCF), Phase 2 (Slab MDI relaxation), Phase 3 (3 progression graphs, Winmostar XYZ, $\\gamma$), Phase 4 (local staging in `nas_staging_periods/{101_0}{N}周期5Å` with bulk files included), Phase 5 (update `SURFACE_ENERGY_RESULTS.md` and `surface_energy_vs_periods_plot_data.csv`).\n- **Sync Scripts**:\n  - `sync_all_2periods_to_nas.py` / `copy_summary_to_nas.py` (can be adapted or expanded for period staging).\n- **Staging Root**: `/home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/nas_staging_periods/`\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Explain the Automation Flow & Slash Command to the User**:\n   - Inform the user that because calculating 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10 periods (up to 360 atoms) takes approximately 3.5〜4.5 hours, the standard and most reliable way to instruct Antigravity is using the `/goal` command:\n     ```text\n     /goal 準備した run_periods_sweep_1_to_10.py を実行して、周期数 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10 のバルク先行計算・スラブ緩和・NAS保存・グラフ更新をすべて完了させてください\n     ```\n2. **Execute the Period Sweep (`run_periods_sweep_1_to_10.py`)**:\n   - Run `/home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_env_rtx5080/bin/python3 run_periods_sweep_1_to_10.py`.\n   - Monitor each condition:\n     - 1 周期 (`{101_0}1周期5Å`, 36 atoms)\n     - 3 周期 (`{101_0}3周期5Å`, 108 atoms)\n     - 5 周期 (`{101_0}5周期5Å`, 180 atoms)\n     - 7 周期 (`{101_0}7周期5Å`, 252 atoms)\n     - 9 周期 (`{101_0}9周期5Å`, 324 atoms)\n     - 10 周期 (`{101_0}10周期5Å`, 360 atoms)\n3. **NAS Batch Sync**:\n   - Create and run `sync_all_periods_to_nas.py` with `BypassSandbox: true` to copy all folders in `nas_staging_periods/` to `\\\\192.168.12.69\\Results\\yamazaki\\research\\{101_0}〇周期5Å`.\n   - Ensure bulk model files (`espresso_bulk_scf.pwi/.pwo`, `bulk_10-10_{natoms}atoms_true_bulk.*`) are present in each folder.\n4. **Update Master Graphs and Records**:\n   - Update [`SURFACE_ENERGY_RESULTS.md`](file:///home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/SURFACE_ENERGY_RESULTS.md) with Cases for periods 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10.\n   - Generate and sync `周期数と表面破壊エネルギーの関係.*` (PNG, PDF, SVG) containing all 10 periods (1 to 10).\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Strict Order (Rule #1)**: True Bulk 1-Point SCF MUST run first and confirm $E_{\\text{bulk}}$ before slab relaxation begins.\n- **Data Bundling**: Bulk model calculation files must be bundled inside each period's output folder alongside slab data.\n- **Folder Naming on NAS**: Must match `{101_0}〇周期5Å` (e.g. `{101_0}1周期5Å`, `{101_0}3周期5Å`, `{101_0}5周期5Å`, etc.).\n- **Physical Cut (Rule #10)**: Cleavage plane must be weak bonds ($dz \\approx 1.776\\text{ \\AA}$), keeping dense pairs at surface boundaries.\n- **Graph Style**: Period comparison graph must adhere to AGENTS.md §7: 5.6×4.4\", open purple triangle markers (`#8A2BE2`, $s=70$), literature line at $3.03\\text{ J/m}^2$, y-axis $2.2 \\sim 3.2\\text{ J/m}^2$, MS Mincho 14.5 pt / Times New Roman 11.5 pt.\n</summary>\n\n# Conversation Logs\nStart with the compact transcript; if a step has `truncated_fields`, read only that specific line in `transcript_full.jsonl`:\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl`\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl`"}
